NexRouter — licensing
=====================

This project is a firmware overlay and tooling layer built on top of OpenWrt.
It intentionally uses different licences for different parts, matching the
licences of what each part sits on. The full text of each licence is included
under LICENSES/.

Firmware overlay and on-device scripts — GPL-2.0-or-later
---------------------------------------------------------
  build/files/**            (UCI defaults, init scripts, the rpcd plugin, the
                             insight-query intelligence layer, sysctl/network
                             config, the shipped OUI table)
  build/build.sh
  build/patches/**

  These are derivative works intended to be combined into an OpenWrt image and
  run on the device alongside GPL'd OpenWrt components. They are licensed
  GPL-2.0-or-later to match OpenWrt. See LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt.

Web user interface — MIT
------------------------
  webui/**

  The dashboard is a standalone static SPA that talks to the router over the
  public ubus JSON-RPC API. It is not linked with GPL code at build or run time,
  so it is released under the permissive MIT licence. See LICENSES/MIT.txt.

Build-time and analysis tooling — MIT
-------------------------------------
  tools/**                  (build-oui.mjs)
  analysis/tools/**         (fwscan.mjs)
  companion/nexinsight/**   (the off-router NetFlow collector and ML companion)

  These run on a build machine or a separate host, not on the router, and are
  standalone tools. MIT. See LICENSES/MIT.txt.

Documentation — CC-BY-4.0
-------------------------
  docs/**, README.md

  Prose and diagrams, shareable with attribution.

Third-party components in a built image
---------------------------------------
An image produced by build/build.sh contains, in addition to the above:

  * OpenWrt base system and packages — GPL-2.0 (and per-package licences)
  * the Linux kernel — GPL-2.0
  * the mt76 wireless driver — ISC
  * jq — MIT
  * the IEEE OUI registry data shipped at build/files/usr/lib/nexrouter/oui.txt
    — derived from the IEEE Registration Authority public OUI listing, which the
    IEEE makes freely available; the derived table here carries no additional
    restriction beyond attribution to the IEEE Registration Authority.

The resulting flash image is therefore a combined work whose licensing is the
union of its components, dominated by the GPL-2.0 of OpenWrt and the kernel.
Nothing in this project relicenses any upstream component.

No trademark claim is made. "Xiaomi", "Redmi", "OpenWrt" and "MediaTek" are the
property of their respective holders; this is an independent, unofficial project
and is not endorsed by or affiliated with any of them.
